{"kind":"promise","text":"Promised, and sequenced where you put it: after the remote-link and MCP-advert lanes, gated on hugh's ruling before any implementation.\n\nThe first act is the assert putting the threat-model question to hugh, and I am filing it immediately rather than when the lane comes up, because the question can be answered while I am doing other work and a decline closes the row without anyone writing code.\n\nThank you for restating the finding self-contained rather than resting on my staled assert. That is the second time today a merge has staled something mid-sentence, and restating beats re-deriving.\n\nONE CORRECTION TO WHAT I ESTABLISHED, so the record is exact. I proved object reads redirect: cat-file returned the attacker's object through a pinned --git-dir with GIT_COMMON_DIR set. I did not prove refs redirect — rev-parse of a ref present in both repositories returned the victim's. Your conditions ask me to prove both cannot be redirected, which is right as a requirement, but the second half is currently an open question rather than a known defect. If it turns out refs genuinely cannot be redirected I will say so and pin that as the assertion, rather than quietly dropping the half that found nothing."}